IMPLEMENTATION NOTES FOR BUILDERS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CRITICAL: These make or break the premium feel:

1. NEVER use pure white backgrounds (#FFFFFF) on any page
   → Use #070711 or #0C0C1E as page backgrounds

2. ALWAYS add purple-tinted shadows to cards
   → Generic black shadows look cheap on dark themes

3. The ambient background glows MUST be implemented
   → They create depth and atmosphere that makes it feel alive
   → Large radial-gradient divs, position:fixed or absolute,
     pointer-events:none, z-index:0

4. Glass morphism needs real backdrop-filter: blur(20px)
   → Test on multiple backgrounds to ensure it reads
   → Fallback for browsers without support: solid dark bg

5. Gradient text (webkit-background-clip) on key headlines
   → "Master Your Skills" / "Career Ready" / key CTAs
   → Background-size 200% + animation for living gradients

6. SVG connector lines MUST be curved cubic bezier
   → Straight lines look like MS Paint diagrams
   → Use: M x1,y1 C cx1,cy1 cx2,cy2 x2,y2

7. Loading skeleton must match dark theme
   → Use rgba(255,255,255,0.04) → rgba(255,255,255,0.08) shimmer
   → NOT gray shimmer (looks wrong on dark)

8. Focus states on dark theme:
   → 2px solid #7C3AED, offset 3px
   → OR: box-shadow 0 0 0 3px rgba(124,58,237,0.4)

9. Scrollbar styling (webkit):
   → scrollbar-width: thin / color: rgba(124,58,237,0.3) transparent

10. Font smoothing:
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale
    (Critical for white text on dark — makes it crisp)